      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T07:32:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this change makes the wait slower than the previous polling loop. Both ways have to wait for all the maps to finish. Between the `MapAsync` calls and the polling starts, there is no other works, hence IMO there is no benefit of splitting the calls.\n\nThere were also 2 more reasons to switch to use `WaitAny` here:\n- Using `ProcessEvent/Tick` wouldn\u0027t be able to catch the bug in the CL. The bug here related to incorrect recycling in D3D11 being triggered by `WaitAny`. It\u0027s not triggered by `ProcessEvent/Tick`.\n- The next CL which adds an option to delay D3D11 flush has a bit longer delay with these Tick() loops. Though it\u0027s not much.\n\nNevertheless, those reasons are minor. I have reverted this change and added a dedicated regression test instead.",
      "parentUuid": "4e3ea1b5_8a4a7e12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1793,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1825,
